{"book":52,"chapter":1,"context":{"chapter":1,"title":"Faith, Love, and Hope at Work","summary":"Paul thanks God for the Thessalonians, who welcomed the gospel despite suffering, turned from idols to the living God, and became an example to believers everywhere.","background":"Thessalonica sat on a major Roman road and had a busy harbor, so news traveled fast; Paul says reports of their faith had spread throughout Macedonia, Achaia and beyond (v. 8). Turning away from the gods was costly in a Greek city, where worship was woven into civic festivals, trade associations and family life. Believers could be seen as disloyal neighbors.","customs":[{"term":"Turning from idols","verses":"1:9","note":"This shows most of the church were Gentiles. Leaving idol worship meant leaving the shared religious life of their city and families."}],"watchFor":["The trio of faith, love and hope (v. 3), which returns in 5:8.","Waiting for God's Son from heaven (v. 10) introduces a major theme of the letter."],"connections":["Acts 17:1-9","1 Corinthians 13:13","Philippians 3:20"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["Παῦλος","Paulos","G3972","N-NSM-P","Paul"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["Σιλουανὸς","Silouanos","G4610","N-NSM-P","Silvanus"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["Τιμόθεος","Timotheos","G5095","N-NSM-P","Timothy"],["τῇ","tēa","G3588","T-DSF","To the"],["ἐκκλησίᾳ","ekklēsia","G1577","N-DSF","church"],["Θεσσαλονικέων","Thessalonikeōn","G2331","N-GPM-LG","of the Thessalonians"],["ἐν","en","G1722","PREP","in"],["θεῷ","theō","G2316","N-DSM-T","God"],["πατρὶ","patri","G3962","N-DSM-T","[the] Father"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["κυρίῳ","kuriō","G2962","N-DSM-T","in [the] Lord"],["Ἰησοῦ","Iēsou","G2424","N-DSM-P","Jesus"],["Χριστῷ·","Christō","G5547","N-DSM-T","Christ"],["χάρις","charis","G5485","N-NSF","Grace"],["ὑμῖν","humin","G4771","P-2DP","to you"],["καὶ","kai","G2532","CONJ","and"],["εἰρήνη","eirēnē","G1515","N-NSF","peace"],["ἀπὸ","apo","G575","PREP","from"],["θεοῦ","theou","